From 353be58196c9304acdcd4cdfb1a4b50974a64a7b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: z060142 <z060142@yahoo.com.tw>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 02:56:36 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 102/119] S8 metering: the meter reads a histogram, because a
 mean cannot survive a sky

decisions/s8-metering.md approach A, part 1: the renderer half.

A new compute pass in CAutoExposureStage bins the quarter-res exposed HDR
source - the same texture the stock measure pass reads, after the round-3
firefly-knee fix - into a 64-bin log2 luminance histogram, 8x8 groups,
groupshared bins, one global InterlockedAdd per bin per group. The window is
-14 to +18 stops relative to MID GREY, half a stop per bin, which is only
possible because the pre-exposure anchors 0.18: it needs no per-scene tuning at
any time of day, which is the one thing UE's absolute HistogramLogMin/Max
cannot do. Bins 0 and 63 saturate, so an Inf gets a POSITION and no magnitude
and the percentile band can ignore it entirely - the runaway of round 2 becomes
structurally impossible rather than clamped away.

What is metered CHANGES, and it is stated in the shader. The stock pass divides
the G-buffer albedo out to estimate illuminance and fabricates rho = 0.2 for
every pixel with no albedo - sky, emissive, everything forward-rendered. That
fabrication is calibrated for midday sun and over-reads by 1.6 to 3.2 stops
otherwise, times the sky's share of the frame. This pass meters luminance, so
the fallback no longer exists and NO LONGER MATTERS: the meter is now a
reflected meter, and what keeps the calibration is the target, not the
quantity. An 18 % card under the light still lands on 0.18 by D6, so
C = 120*pi from s1-exposure-constant.md holds unchanged.

Metering Mode rides the post-effect bus as the accumulation weight: Average,
CenterWeighted (a smooth radial falloff, 100 % centre to 25 % corner) and Spot
(a soft-edged disc a fifth of the frame height across). The falloff is smooth
because a hard edge makes the exposure step as content crosses it.

The readback is the two-phase path we already had, with a new decode. The
histogram accumulates into a 64x1 TEXTURE and not a CGpuBuffer, because
DownloadToStagingResource lives on CDeviceTexture and has no buffer twin
anywhere in this tree. ETEX_Format has no uint entry, so the target is eTF_R32F
with FT_USAGE_UAV_RWTEXTURE - which makes the resource R32_TYPELESS - plus a
hand-built DXGI_FORMAT_R32_UINT view, exactly as m_pTexLinearDepthFixupUAV
already does. 256 bytes and one fence a frame instead of four bytes and one
fence; the latency is unchanged and invisible against tau.

r_SceneReferredMeterHistogram (default 1) keeps the shipped whole-frame
log-mean alive at 0 as a runtime A/B and as the fallback if the compute pass
ever misbehaves - which is also why the meter's 14-stop ceiling stays in the
shader. It no longer touches the metering that ships.

EFQ_GetSceneReferredMeterHistogram hands the bins to the camera by value, with
the pre-exposure of the sampled frame and the window travelling beside them so
no consumer has to keep a second copy of either in step.

